<LessonLayout title="Workbook &mdash; The Holy Spirit" cic="CCC 683-747" scripture="">

<section class="content">

<h2>Student Workbook</h2>
<p class="big-question">For use after class or in a group. Print this page or work in your notebook.</p>

<h3>Remembering the Essentials</h3>

<ol>
<li>Who is the Holy Spirit? Is it a force, an energy, or a Person?</li>
<li>What does the word &laquo;Paraclete&raquo; mean and why does Jesus use it to refer to the Holy Spirit?</li>
<li>Name the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit.</li>
<li>What happened at Pentecost and why is it important for the Church?</li>
<li>According to Romans 8:26, what does the Holy Spirit do when we do not know how to pray?</li>
</ol>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>For Reflection and Writing</h3>

<p>Answer each question honestly. There are no &laquo;correct&raquo; answers to these personal questions.</p>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">1. What image of the Holy Spirit did you have before this class? How does knowing that he is a Person who dwells in you change things?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think about what you thought of the Holy Spirit: was it something vague, a dove, a force? Now imagine that he is someone concrete who lives within you.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">2. Of the seven gifts of the Holy Spirit, which one do you feel you need most right now? Why?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Wisdom, understanding, counsel, fortitude, knowledge, piety, fear of the Lord. Which one are you lacking?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">3. The fruits of the Spirit are &laquo;love, joy, peace, patience, kindness, goodness, faithfulness, gentleness, self-control.&raquo; Which one is most visible in your life? Which one would you like to grow?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Be honest: where do you see good fruit? Where do you feel there is dryness?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">4. Have you ever felt that you did not know how to pray, but something within you was praying? Tell about it.</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Romans 8:26 says that the Spirit &laquo;intercedes for us with groanings too deep for words.&raquo; Sometimes the Spirit prays in us without words.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

<div class="question-block">
<p class="question-block__q">5. If the Holy Spirit truly dwells in you, what concrete decision can you make this week to give him more space?</p>
<p class="question-block__p">Think of something specific: a prayer, an act of charity, forgiving someone, seeking counsel...</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content" id="activities">

<h3>Practical Activities</h3>

<h4>A. Fruit inventory</h4>
<p>Write out the list of the fruits of the Spirit (Gal 5:22-23). Next to each fruit, put a mark: ✓ if you see it growing in your life, ? if you are not sure, ✗ if you feel it needs attention. Then choose one fruit you want to cultivate this week and write a concrete action.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>B. Pray the sequence &laquo;Veni Sancte Spiritus&raquo;</h4>
<p>Look up the Pentecost sequence (you can find it online). Read it slowly, phrase by phrase. Underline the phrases that touch you most. What are you asking the Holy Spirit?</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

<h4>C. Daily prayer to the Holy Spirit</h4>
<p>This week, before every important decision, pause and say: &laquo;Come, Holy Spirit.&raquo; Keep a record: date, situation, and what you felt afterward.</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);margin-bottom:8px">&nbsp;</p>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Memory Verse</h3>

<div class="bible-passage">
<p>&laquo;The Spirit helps us in our weakness, for we do not know how to pray as we ought, but the Spirit himself intercedes for us with groanings too deep for words.&raquo;</p>
<p class="bible-passage__ref">&mdash; Romans 8:26</p>
</div>

</section>

<section class="content">

<h3>Prayer for This Week</h3>

<blockquote>
<p>Come, Holy Spirit,<br />
come into my heart,<br />
give me your light to know the way,<br />
give me your strength to follow it,<br />
give me your love to live it.<br />
May I not walk alone,<br />
may I not speak without listening,<br />
may I not decide without seeking your will.<br />
Fill my life with your fruits:<br />
love, joy, peace, patience.<br />
And make me your instrument.<br />
Amen.</p>
</blockquote>

</section>

